      "finalText": "Review complete for PR **9101** at `10bfa73cdbee1025a1466d6247d879ebe3d6b56e`. **Verdict: FAIL** (posted via `post_verdict` with blocking `never-expires`).\n\n### What changed\n\n`_eligible_for_removal` gates removal of deregistered subnets after **`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (48h)** (**measured** at head). The PR swaps:\n\n- **Base:** `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`\n- **Head:** `elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`\n\nIn Python, **`timedelta.seconds` is only the fraction of the delta within a single day** (0–86399), not total elapsed time (**measured**). **`total_seconds()`** is the full duration. Because `172800` is two full days, comparing `.seconds` to `172800` can never succeed: `.seconds` is always `< 86400`.\n\n**Entry path (**inferred**):** `_compute_membership` and `_shrink_allowed` both call `_eligible_for_removal`; if it never returns true after grace, negative netuids never drop and the universe never shrinks on schedule.\n\n### Deregistered subnet: base vs head\n\nAssume a non-root netuid with `probe is False` and a valid `negative_since` (already deregistered). Only the grace comparison differs:\n\n| Elapsed since `negative_since` | Base (`total_seconds() >= 172800`) | Head (`elapsed.seconds >= 172800`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **23h** (below 24h) | Not eligible | Not eligible |\n| **25h** (above 24h, still under 48h) | Not eligible | Not eligible |\n| **47h** (below 48h) | Not eligible | Not eligible |\n| **48h** (at grace) | **Eligible for removal** | **Not eligible** (`days=2`, `seconds=0`) |\n| **49h** (above 48h) | **Eligible** | **Not eligible** (`seconds=3600`) |\n| **72h** | **Eligible** | **Not eligible** (`seconds=0`) |\n\nSo around **24h** both implementations behave the same (still inside grace). Around **48h**, base allows removal once full grace has passed; **head never allows removal** after any multi-day elapsed time—deregistered subnets effectively **never expire** from membership.\n\n**Fix:** restore `total_seconds()`, or compare `elapsed >= timedelta(seconds=STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)`.\n\nGate `next` after verdict: **`review`** (fixture still shows MC as missing; verdict was recorded with `reason: eval`).",
