            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line filter on `_compute_membership` output: `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, skipping falsy int keys (netuid **0**). **Measured** intent aligns with `load_membership_receipt` / `membership_scoring_expected`, which already treat `int(n) > 0` as the scoring/API surface and expose `root_netuid_in_membership` telemetry.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Built membership can omit 0 while `_shrink_allowed` forbids dropping it (MODIFY)\n\n**Measured** (`internal/subnet_universe.py`):\n- `ROOT_NETUID = 0`; when `observed_members` is non-empty, `candidates.add(ROOT_NETUID)` and netuid 0 can remain in `validity_map` under key `\"0\"`.\n- `_eligible_for_removal` returns **False** for `netuid == ROOT_NETUID` always.\n- `_shrink_allowed` requires drop evidence for every netuid in `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.snapshot.netuids)`.\n- `refresh_once` replaces the build with `_hold_prior(...)` when shrink is not allowed.\n\n**Inferred**: Before this diff, `netuids` was derived from all `validity_map` keys, so a persisted LKG that included **0** in `netuids` stayed self-consistent across refreshes. After this diff, the built snapshot **always** omits 0 from `netuids` while `validity_map` may still contain `\"0\"`. Any prior snapshot whose `netuids` tuple still contains 0 triggers a shrink check that **cannot** succeed for that removal (root is never eligible). The worker then **publishes the prior snapshot unchanged** every cycle instead of the newly computed membership.\n\nThat is not an overflow/NaN path and does not abort the refresh thread (**measured**: exception is not raised; hold path is explicit). It **does** mean later cycles keep serving a membership list that still contains root even though `_compute_membership` now tries to drop it — the fix does not land until the LKG no longer lists 0 (manual persist or one-time migration). **poisons-later-row** applies: stale root-in-membership state survives refresh cycles.\n\n**Suggested fix (minimal)**: Treat omitting `ROOT_NETUID` from `netuids` as a safe shrink (exclude 0 from the `_shrink_allowed` removed set, and/or drop the `\"0\"` entry from `validity_map` when building the snapshot). Optionally normalize on load in `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`.\n\n### P3 — Double `int(k)` per key\n\n**Inferred**: Minor; use a walrus/comprehension helper if touched again.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured** in `snapshot_coverage.py`: root is never scored; membership denominator uses `int(n) > 0`. This diff moves shared `snap.netuids` toward that contract. **Inferred**: Owner “chain wins / grace” rules are unchanged; no new float paths.\n\n## Settled-check\n\n**guess**: No roadmap/docs in this fixture slice for “placeholder keys”; shrink-vs-root interaction is not settled in-repo here.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial)\n\n**Measured**: Non-numeric `validity_map` keys still make `int(k)` raise in this comprehension (same as base). **Inferred**: `1e308` / NaN not in play (string keys from `str(netuid)` only in the loop).\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | shrink-hold vs root omission; int(k) on map keys | — |\n| owner-rules | root excluded from scoring surface | — |\n| settled-check | no settled doc on placeholder/shrink | — |",
