          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR replaces the **chain-wins** branch in `_merge_sources` with a **dispute / keep positive** path when TaoMarketCap lists a netuid (`tmc_positive is True`) but a complete registration probe does not (`probe_positive is False`). That inverts the pinned membership contract for this review.\n\n## Pinned contract (session)\n\n- **measured (user pin):** A definitive chain negative (complete chain read that does not list the netuid) **beats** a TaoMarketCap listing.\n- **measured (user pin):** A chain read that fails, times out, or is unknown is **not** a negative.\n\n## What changed (**measured** from diff at `1748ed8`)\n\n**Base** handled `probe_positive is False and tmc_positive is not False` by returning `validity=\"negative\"`, setting `negative_since`, and treating TMC-true as `disputed` while still starting the grace clock toward removal.\n\n**Head** handles only `tmc_positive is True and probe_positive is False` by returning `validity=\"positive\"`, `disputed=True`, `negative_since=None` — so the netuid **stays in** `validity_map` and never enters `_eligible_for_removal` on that cycle’s chain evidence alone.\n\n## Entry-point trace (**inferred** from `internal/subnet_universe.py` at head)\n\nProduction path: `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources`.\n\nRemoval requires `validity == \"negative\"` **and** `_eligible_for_removal` (probe `False`, `negative_since` set, ≥ `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`). With head logic, **TMC+ / probe−** never sets `negative_since`, so a chain-confirmed deregistration while TMC still lists the subnet does not begin the 48h removal path.\n\n## Secondary regression (**inferred**)\n\nThe deleted condition was `tmc_positive is not False` (includes `None`). **Head** no longer maps **probe− / TMC incomplete (`None`)** to immediate negative; that case falls into the generic `tmc_positive is None or probe_positive is None` branch and **retains prior validity** instead of applying a fresh chain negative. That also diverges from the prior owner-rule comment on base and from the pinned “definitive chain negative” rule (probe succeeded; TMC incompleteness is not a chain failure).\n\n## Severities\n\n| Finding | Severity | Blocking tag |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Chain definitive negative no longer beats TMC listing (dispute keeps member, no grace) | P1 | `never-expires` |\n| Chain negative + incomplete TMC no longer starts negative / grace | P2 | — (same policy drift) |\n| Owner-rule comment removed without replacement stating new precedence | P2 | — |\n\n## Requested direction\n\nEither restore chain-wins for **complete probe False** (still honoring “failed/unknown chain read is not negative”), or obtain an explicit owner decision that **dispute-positive** supersedes chain removal — plus tests covering TMC+/probe− and probe−/TMC-unknown.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `refresh_once`→`_merge_sources`; probe−+TMC+ stays positive, no `negative_since` | — |\n| owner-rules | Base comment: chain wins on complete probe−; head removes that branch | — |\n| settled-check | Fixture repo has no roadmap/docs entry settling dispute-over-chain; treat as open policy change | — |",
            "headSha": "1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001",
            "blocking": [
