            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR adds a `(config: …)` suffix to the TMC fetch failure warning by copying every `TMC*` / `TAOMARKETCAP*` environment variable **with its value** into the log line. Staging already demonstrated the outcome: a failed fetch log carries `TMC_API_KEY` in plaintext. That is a credential leak into log aggregation, not a safe debugging aid.\n\n## Trace (real entry point)\n\n**Measured:** `_default_tmc_fetch` in `internal/subnet_universe.py` is the default `SnapshotBuilder._tmc_fetch`; on any exception it now builds `tmc_env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k.upper().startswith((\"TMC\", \"TAOMARKETCAP\"))}` and logs it via `logger.warning(..., exc, tmc_env)` before returning `set(), {}, False` (incomplete TMC, prior-universe retention unchanged).\n\n**Inferred:** Upstream errors such as HTTP 502 still take this path; every intermittent TMC outage becomes an automatic secret exfiltration event to whatever collects worker warnings.\n\n**Measured (author report):** Staging log line `subnet_universe TMC fetch failed: upstream 502 (config: {…})` included the live `TMC_API_KEY` value — consistent with the new code and not repeatable here in the verdict body.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Severity | Label | Finding |\n|----|----------|-------|---------|\n| F1 | P0 | **measured** + **inferred** | Logging full `tmc_env` values on failure exposes secrets (`TMC_API_KEY`, any `TAOMARKETCAP*` tokens). Confirmed in staging by the pasted failure log. |\n| F2 | P2 | **inferred** | Safe ops signal needs **names only** or redacted placeholders (e.g. key present/missing, base URL), never secret values. |\n\nUniverse membership behavior on incomplete TMC remains hold-prior / degraded paths; this change does not introduce never-expire, float overflow, cycle abort, or row-poison bugs in the membership map — the defect is logging only.\n\n## Required fix direction\n\nRemove value emission from logs. Log allowed non-secret settings (URL, timeout flags) explicitly, or log env **keys** and whether each is set, with values replaced by a constant redaction token.\n\nRotate any `TMC_API_KEY` that appeared in staging logs after merge/deploy of this behavior.",
