          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: drop `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` so any JSON object dict is parsed via `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`, matching the PR intent to pick up worker-published snapshots that legitimately have empty membership (`netuids: []` or missing key).\n\n## Trace (real entry: `ensure_universe_reader` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale`)\n\n**Measured:** Diff removes only the empty/falsy-`netuids` early return; `isinstance(payload, dict)` guard remains; `json.load` / `from_dict` failures still hit the existing `except` and return the in-memory `_snapshot` without updating `_disk_mtime`.\n\n**Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` builds `netuids` with `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []`, coerces with `int(n)`, and filters row dicts — non-numeric netuid elements raise and trigger the same fallback (**inferred** from control flow, not executed).\n\n**Inferred:** A persisted empty-but-well-formed snapshot (worker `_atomic_persist` after an intentional empty membership build) now replaces stale in-memory LKG on mtime bump; previously the web reader ignored that file and kept an older non-empty snapshot — the bug this PR fixes.\n\n**Inferred:** `get_lkg_or_emergency()` still substitutes `emergency_registry` when `not snap.netuids`, so call sites using that helper do not silently serve an empty universe as “approved” membership.\n\n**Inferred:** `load_membership_receipt` / phase-1 admission gates fail closed on empty `expected_netuids`, degraded, or stale receipts — no new path that admits scoring from a corrupt empty dict without going through existing receipt rules.\n\n## Non-blocking notes (P3)\n\n**Inferred:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `payload.get(\"netuids\")` on cold start while hot reload no longer does — intentional asymmetry is plausible (missing file → emergency; worker publish → trust disk) but worth a one-line comment if authors want parity documented.\n\n## Blocking categories\n\nNone of `never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, or `poisons-later-row` apply: grace/removal logic in `_compute_membership` / `_eligible_for_removal` is untouched, and reload does not introduce new float paths or cycle aborts.",
