            "body": "## SimiBot comment → counted head (trace)\n\n**Measured** on `review-gate-bot/bot/lib/verdicts.ts` at head `2dee2723…`:\n\n1. `collectPinnedVerdicts` hits the SimiBot branch when `simibotMcHead(comment)` is defined: login `simibot[bot]`, App id `5501340`, exactly one `<!-- mc-verdict:<40-hex> -->` (`MC_VERDICT_MARKER`).\n2. Verdict token comes from `verdictFromComment` → `parseVerdictToken` → first non-empty line after stripping HTML comments; for `PASS`, `passTailAllowed(tail)` must return true or the comment yields **no** verdict (`noteUnparsed`, no pin).\n3. When a verdict is parsed, the pinned record uses **`headSha: simibotHead` from the marker only**. The first-line SHA (if any) is **not** read for pinning and **not** compared to the marker.\n\nSo a SimiBot comment that parses as `PASS` is counted at the marker’s full SHA, regardless of a different SHA in the `PASS` tail.\n\n## Findings vs pinned rule (this round)\n\n**P1 — Pointer/marker agreement missing (fail-closed gap).** Pinned rule: the first-line pointer (full 40-hex or ≥12-hex prefix that resolves to the head) must equal the `mc-verdict` marker head; disagreement → **no verdict**. **Measured:** the SimiBot branch never extracts the tail pointer or calls `resolveSha`; it always pins to `simibotHead` when `passTailAllowed` passes. **Inferred:** `PASS at <other-sha>` + marker for the PR head still records an MC verdict at the marker head — a false release if the line and marker diverge.\n\n**P2 — Tail SHA allowlist vs 12-hex floor.** Pinned rule requires ≥12 hex for abbreviated pointers (same rationale as `shaClaimedByComment` / `CLAIM_PATTERNS`). **Measured:** `SHA_WORD` is `/^[0-9a-f]{7,40}$/i` inside `passTailAllowed`, so 7–11 character “pointers” are syntactically allowed on the first line without resolution or marker check.\n\n**P3 — Extra keyword `on`.** **Measured:** `passTailAllowed` accepts `PASS on <sha>` via `keyword === \"on\"`. **Inferred:** broader surface than the pinned forms (`at`, `at head`, `head`, bare SHA); not necessarily wrong but undocumented vs this round’s rule.\n\n## What improved\n\n**Measured:** Replacing `WITHDRAWN` with `passTailAllowed` correctly rejects caveat tails such as `PASS, but …` (no verdict). **Measured:** Dedicated SimiBot path with `mc-verdict` marker before `subnet-review-gate:mc-verdict` markers is the right shape for SimiBot-authored MC comments.\n\n## Required follow-up\n\nIn the SimiBot branch (after a parsed verdict): parse the optional first-line pointer; require full-40 equality to `simibotHead`, or 12–39 hex resolved via `input.resolveSha` to `simibotHead`; if a pointer is present and disagrees, treat as **no verdict** (do not push); align minimum prefix length with 12, not 7.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | SimiBot pin ignores first-line SHA; disagreement still counts | — |\n| owner-rules | Fail-closed / no stale PASS — pointer must bind to head | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: fixture has no locks/roadmap for this bot-only diff | — |",
