            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe move from a withdrawal regex to `passTailAllowed` is the right shape: fail-closed allowlist, caveats like `PASS, not approved` no longer parse (**measured** on the parser logic in `verdicts.ts`). SimiBot MC handling via `simibotMcHead` and `<!-- mc-verdict:<sha> -->` is wired before the subnet-review-gate marker path (**measured**).\n\n## Finding (P2)\n\n**`SHA_WORD` still accepts 7–11 hex “words” as tail pointers**, which conflicts with the pinned pointer rule and with the same file’s claim logic.\n\nIn `passTailAllowed`, tail SHAs are validated with:\n\n`const SHA_WORD = /^[0-9a-f]{7,40}$/i;`\n\nSo these tails still **parse as PASS** (**inferred** from the function, not executed here):\n\n| Example tail | Why it should not count as a pointer | Current parser |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `deadbeef` | 8 hex letters, English word, not a 40-char SHA or ≥12 prefix | **Accepted** as bare SHA word |\n| `effaced` | 7 hex letters, same class | **Accepted** |\n| `abcdef12345` | 11-char prefix (<12) | **Accepted** |\n| `head abcdef1` | 7-char fragment after `head` | **Accepted** |\n\nThe file already documents the 12-character floor for abbreviated *claims* in `shaClaimedByComment` (“Twelve, not GitHub’s seven…”) (**measured**). Tail validation should match: **40-char full SHA, or 12–39 hex only**—not GitHub’s 7-character short form and not hex-looking English words in the 7–11 range.\n\n**Why this matters for the gate:** For Cursor/Ditto, a bogus tail often fails pinning later (**inferred**), so the slot may stall silently. For **MC via SimiBot** (or any path where `headSha` comes from `<!-- mc-verdict:… -->` / `subnet-review-gate:mc-verdict:…`), `parseVerdictToken` is the only tail check: `PASS deadbeef` with a valid marker would still record **mc PASS** (**inferred**). That is exactly the class of “word after PASS that is not a pointer” this PR is meant to reject.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Split tail SHA validation from claim patterns—e.g. accept only `^[0-9a-f]{40}$` or `^[0-9a-f]{12,39}$` (case as you prefer), and add unit cases for `deadbeef`, `effaced`, 11-char prefixes, and `deadbeef/effaced` if you normalize `/` in the tail. Keep bare `PASS`, pointer forms (`at`, `at head`, `head`, `on`), and optional `-grokbot`/`-simibot` as today.\n\n## What looked fine\n\n- Allowlist rejects prose caveats (`PASS, but …`, `PASS not approved`) (**inferred** from structure).\n- `MODIFY`/`FAIL` tails are not filtered by `passTailAllowed` (**measured**).\n- No float/cycle row semantics in this diff (**measured**).\n\n## Labels\n\n- P2 finding: **inferred** (read-path analysis; no test run in this session).\n- File text / diff: **measured** via `get_pr_diff` and `read_repo_file` at `2dee2723…`.",
