            "body": "## Summary\n\nMechanical extraction of ISO timestamp parsing from `_eligible_for_removal` into `_parse_utc`. **Measured:** diff at `598ca721f1154e9e5908e2928d05c00cf0409ba5` touches `internal/subnet_universe.py` and one focused unit test.\n\n## Entry-point trace (inferred from head file reads)\n\nRemoval still flows: `_compute_membership` builds `DropEvidence(negative_since=…)` from `_merge_sources`, then calls `_eligible_for_removal(netuid, evidence, now)` when `validity == \"negative\"`. Shrink gating in `_shrink_allowed` uses the same helper. The only change on that path is delegating parse/normalize to `_parse_utc` instead of inline `try/except` around `datetime.fromisoformat(str(...))` plus naive→UTC `replace`.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n| Input shape | Effect on removal | vs base |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Valid ISO from `_now_iso()` / tests | Grace elapsed when `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` | Same |\n| `None`, garbage, `str(None)`→unparseable | `_parse_utc` → `None` → not eligible | Same as prior `except` → `False` |\n| Empty / missing `negative_since` | Guard `if not evidence.negative_since` before parse | Unchanged |\n| Naive ISO | Assumed UTC via `replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)` | Unchanged; new test **measured** in diff |\n\nNo new path accepts `1e308`, bools-as-numbers, or other non-ISO scalars into arithmetic beyond `str(value)` + `fromisoformat`, which is what base already did. No new multiply that could overflow to `inf` on the grace check.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured:** `_merge_sources` chain-wins / grace-clock comments and logic are untouched. This diff does not alter when `negative_since` is set or how chain vs TMC disputes resolve.\n\n## Settled / not new\n\nUnparseable persisted `negative_since` still blocks removal eligibility (subnet stays until a parsable clock exists). That stuck state predates this refactor; extracting `_parse_utc` does not widen accepted formats or change failure handling.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nTried to break removal/grace semantics via corrupt timestamps and naive ISO; behavior matches inline parser. Test adds direct coverage without changing production call sites beyond the helper.",
