            "body": "## Summary\n\nThree-line observability addition in `refresh_once` after shrink is allowed and before `_publish`: compute `removed = sorted(set(self._snapshot.netuids) - set(built.netuids))`, and if non-empty emit one `logger.info` with the count and the list.\n\n## What the new log line can contain (secrets?)\n\n**Measured:** The format is fixed prose plus two interpolation values:\n\n`subnet_universe removed %d netuid(s) after the 48h grace: %s` with `len(removed)` and `removed`.\n\n`removed` is **only** a sorted list of integers from the set difference between the prior snapshot’s `netuids` tuple and the `built` snapshot’s `netuids` tuple (`internal/subnet_universe.py` at head). No API keys, env vars, RPC payloads, registry row bodies, `validity_map`, or persisted JSON are passed to the logger.\n\n**Inferred:** Log aggregators still see public subnet identifiers (netuid integers), not credential material. This matches the existing unsafe-shrink **warning** on the line above, which already logs the same `removed` list when shrink is blocked.\n\n## How often it can fire\n\n**Measured:** The `logger.info` runs at most **once per** `refresh_once` call that reaches `_publish`, and only when `removed` is non-empty. It does not run when `refresh_once` returns early (non-writer reload, failed non-blocking `_refresh_lock`), when emergency or unsafe-shrink paths call `_hold_prior` (those restore prior `netuids`, so `removed` is empty), or when the refresh does not shrink membership.\n\n**Measured:** On the worker, `_refresh_loop` sleeps `REFRESH_INTERVAL_SECONDS` (300) between loop iterations; each iteration calls `refresh_once`. `kick_refresh_async` can trigger additional `refresh_once` calls.\n\n**Inferred:** In steady state you get **zero** lines while membership is stable; bursts of at most **one line per successful refresh** that actually publishes a strict subset of the prior universe (often spaced by the refresh interval unless kicked).\n\n## Most netuids one line can list\n\n**Measured:** One log emission includes **the full** `removed` list in a single `%s` — no chunking.\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID` (0) is never eligible for removal (`_eligible_for_removal` returns False for netuid 0), and `_shrink_allowed` requires every dropped netuid to pass that gate. So a single line lists every netuid dropped in that publish, upper bounded by `len(prior.netuids) - 1` when root stays in the prior universe, or `len(prior.netuids)` if root were absent from prior (unusual).\n\n**Inferred:** There is no hard cap of `MAX_NETUIDS` (200) on membership size in this log; the list length is whatever the prior universe minus the published universe is for that cycle (typically on the order of live subnet count, not probe scan width).\n\n## Review\n\n**Measured:** No change to membership logic, persistence, or grace — logging only after `_shrink_allowed` has already passed.\n\nNo blocking findings (no never-expires, overflow, aborts-cycle, or poisons-later-row paths introduced).\n",
