      "sessionId": "ses_a37771b1112c20148ea52dd4",
      "finalText": "## What the gate says (measured)\n\nAt head `97e47864ba176a86265a932dc9e7e8e9a1c4ba96` on PR [#9303](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9303), `check_gate_state` reports:\n\n| Reviewer | Verdict at this head |\n|----------|----------------------|\n| MC | PASS |\n| Cursor | **MODIFY** |\n| Ditto | PASS |\n| Replit | missing |\n| Full suite | missing |\n| Replit tagged | no |\n\n**Single allowed next step:** `await_cursor_ditto`\n\n---\n\n## Teammate’s claim vs gate logic\n\n**Inferred:** “Newest verdict wins” is not how this gate works. Each step in the order must be **PASS at the current head**. A later Ditto PASS does not erase an earlier Cursor MODIFY on the same SHA.\n\n**Measured:** The plain order is MC PASS → **Cursor PASS** → Ditto PASS → clean suite → tag Replit → Replit PASS → mergeable. Ditto is already PASS; Cursor is not PASS (MODIFY counts as not satisfied for that slot).\n\nSo you should **not** run the suite, tag Replit, or treat the PR as merge-ready on the basis of Ditto alone. The gate is waiting on **Cursor PASS at this head** (MODIFY must be resolved with a new Cursor verdict that is PASS, or the head must change and the whole chain resets).\n\nMC already has PASS at this head; I am not posting another MC verdict (one per head).\n\n**Inferred:** If Cursor’s MODIFY reflects real issues, those still need to be addressed or re-reviewed at Cursor before the gate advances—chronology among reviewers does not override the fixed order.",
