            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR removes two GitHub reads that were deliberate guards against multi-process posting without KV compare-and-swap. That trade is not safe for `postVerdictComment` on the hosted runtime described in `lock.ts`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `postVerdictComment`: guard 3 removed while non-CAS cross-process races remain (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** The diff deletes the immediate pre-write `alreadyPosted(...)` re-read and the `lostToRecheck` / `already-posted` outcome path. `lock.ts` at head still states that `ctx.host.kv` uses plain get/put, `supportsKvCas` is false in hosted runtime, and that “A genuine simultaneous race between two processes can still post twice.” It also still documents that `postVerdictComment` re-reads immediately before posting to shrink that window — behavior this PR removes without updating `lock.ts`.\n\n**Measured:** `gate.ts` `verdictAt` keeps the **latest** MC verdict at a head when multiple exist.\n\n**Inferred:** Two processes can both pass the initial `alreadyDone()` inside `ranOnce`, both win overlapping claims (documented best-effort edge without CAS), and both enter `run()` without the removed re-read. Both can `createComment` with different verdict bodies for the same head marker. The gate then honors whichever comment sorts last — a MODIFY can be overwritten by a stale PASS or vice versa. That is bad state consumed by later gate steps (`poisons-later-row`), not a harmless duplicate.\n\nThe remaining `isStale()` pull before post does not substitute for guard 3: it addresses head movement/draft, not “another process just landed the marker between claim and write.”\n\n### P2 — `postSlotOnce`: `isStale()` removed before tag writes (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** The diff removes the pre-post `isStale()` check for `@cursor`/`@ditto`/`@replit` slot comments. `postSlotOnce` still documents `superseded` as “PR moved off headSha or turned draft,” but `superseded` is never set in that function after this change (**measured** at head).\n\n**Inferred:** A delivery that read gate state at `headSha`, then loses to a push or draft flip before `createComment`, can still post a tag naming the stale SHA. That matches the failure mode called out in the PR brief (post in flight while head moves). It does not close the stale-head window the old read did.\n\n### P3 — Stale documentation at head (**measured**)\n\n**Measured:** `postVerdictComment`’s block comment still lists three guards including “re-read of the PR’s comments as the last thing before the post.” The file-level comment still says `postVerdictComment` re-reads immediately before posting. Code no longer does guard 3.\n\n## What would make this acceptable\n\nKeep at least the pre-write `alreadyPosted` re-read for `postVerdictComment` (and align docs in `tag.ts` / `lock.ts`), or introduce a real CAS/compare on the system of record. Restoring `isStale()` in `postSlotOnce` before tag posts addresses the push-during-flight tag case without reintroducing the verdict re-read twice elsewhere.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `ranOnce` → `claim` → `run` → `postComment`; cross-process no-CAS path from `lock.ts`; gate consumes latest MC via `verdictAt` | — |\n| owner-rules | Correctness of gate side effects must match documented guarantees; docs must not claim guards that were removed | — |\n| settled-check | No settled decision found in fixture to bless dropping these reads for hosted multi-process KV | — |",
