eady published, prior is already shrunk—cycle 2 keeps those netuids out. If this is the first cycle-2 run at 49h from the T0 poisoned prior, behavior matches the 48h row: grace satisfied, members **dropped**. |\n\nCorrect behavior under the pinned contract at all three times (**inferred** vs base): `probe_val=None` → incomplete-read branch retains prior validity and **does not** advance a deregistration clock; membership stays last-good.\n\n## Blocking\n\n`poisons-later-row`: a failed read writes `negative_since` and negative validity that cycle 2 reads back and uses to drop rows after grace.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `probe_val` → `_merge_sources` → `DropEvidence` → `_eligible_for_removal` / `_shrink_allowed` on the real `SnapshotBuilder.build` path | — |\n| owner-rules | Failed chain read must not start grace; complete chain \"not listed\" may | — |\n| settled-check | Base `probe_val=None` + `_merge_sources` None-handling already settled incomplete probe as unobserved | — |",
