            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR title says it simplifies the 48h grace comparison in `_eligible_for_removal`, but the head replaces `(now - started).total_seconds()` with `elapsed.seconds`. That is not equivalent: `timedelta.seconds` is only the seconds **after** whole days are removed (always `0 <= seconds < 86400`), while `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` is **172800** (48h) per **measured** read of `internal/subnet_universe.py` at head.\n\n**inferred:** `elapsed.seconds >= 172800` is never satisfied for any non-negative elapsed duration, so `_eligible_for_removal` always returns `False` once the other guards pass. **measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires `_eligible_for_removal` for every dropped netuid before membership may shrink; deregistered subnets therefore never become removal-eligible on this head → universe rows **never expire** through the shrink path.\n\n## Concrete elapsed times (deregistered subnet: `probe is False`, valid `negative_since`, non-root)\n\nAssume `started` fixed and `now = started + Δ`. Compare base `(now-started).total_seconds() >= 172800` vs head `elapsed.seconds >= 172800`.\n\n| Elapsed Δ | total_seconds (base uses) | Base eligible? | elapsed.seconds (head uses) | Head eligible? |\n|---|---:|---|---:|---|\n| 23h 59m 59s | 86,399 | No | 86,399 | No |\n| 24h 00m 00s | 86,400 | No | **0** (1 full day) | No |\n| 24h 00m 01s | 86,401 | No | 1 | No |\n| 47h 59m 59s | 172,799 | No | 86,399 | No |\n| **48h 00m 00s** | **172,800** | **Yes** | **0** (2 full days) | **No** |\n| 48h 00m 01s | 172,801 | Yes | 1 | No |\n\n**inferred:** On both sides of **24h**, base and head agree (still below 48h grace). On **48h**, base correctly flips to eligible; head stays ineligible and continues to stay ineligible for all longer durations because `.seconds` never reaches 172800.\n\n## Entry-point trace\n\n**measured:** `_shrink_allowed` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`) loops netuids in `prior.netuids - build.snapshot.netuids` and requires `_eligible_for_removal(netuid, evidence, now)` for each. The changed comparison is on the real removal gate, not a dead helper.\n\n## Required fix direction\n\nRestore total-duration comparison, e.g. `elapsed.total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (or an equivalent that counts whole days), and add a regression test at exactly 48h elapsed.\n\nNo blocking overflow/NaN path introduced by this one-line swap; the defect is pure duration semantics.",
            "skills": [
