            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `_compute_membership`: build `netuids` from `validity_map` keys with `if int(k)`, skipping `0`. That matches how downstream already treats membership (`snapshot_coverage` uses `int(n) > 0`; root is tracked separately in `validity_map` with `ROOT_NETUID = 0`).\n\n## Finding (P2) — shrink gate blocks the fix on existing LKG\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` now returns `netuids` without `0` while `validity_map` can still contain `\"0\"` when root is in `candidates` (`observed_members` → `candidates.add(ROOT_NETUID)`).\n\n**Measured:** `refresh_once` rejects the build when `_shrink_allowed` is false and calls `_hold_prior`, keeping the prior `netuids`/`rows`/`validity_map` unchanged.\n\n**Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires `build.dropped.get(netuid)` with eligible removal evidence for every netuid in `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.snapshot.netuids)`.\n\n**Measured:** `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID` (0), so `0` is never in `dropped`.\n\n**Inferred:** Any persisted snapshot whose `netuids` still include `0` (produced by the pre-fix line `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`) will, on the next worker refresh, produce a build whose membership list omits `0` but carries no drop evidence for `0`. Shrink is blocked, LKG is retained, and `/api/subnets` / `get_netuids()` keep serving `0` until something else rewrites persistence. The new filter never lands in production for those snapshots.\n\n**Suggestion:** Treat root-only list shrink as safe (e.g. skip `ROOT_NETUID` in the `_shrink_allowed` loop, or allow publishing when the only removed IDs are `0`), or normalize `0` out of `prior.netuids` once when loading/building so the guard is not tripped.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n- **`int(k)` on map keys:** Non-numeric keys still raise `ValueError` in the comprehension (same as before). Digit keys behave as before except `\"0\"` / `\"00\"` are omitted (**inferred**).\n- **Empty `netuids` when map is only `\"0\"`:** Triggers existing empty-membership branches in `SnapshotBuilder.build` (**measured**); not new overflow/expiry logic.\n- **Float-like keys:** Not expected from `str(netuid)` keys in the loop (**inferred**).\n\n## Owner rules\n\nNo change to chain-wins removal, 48h grace, or emergency registry semantics. Aligns with “root is not scored / not a subnet row” already encoded in `load_membership_receipt` and `_emergency_rows`.\n\n## Settled\n\nExcluding root from scoring denominators is already settled in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`; this diff extends that idea to the shared universe list builder—reasonable, but the shrink gate migration gap above needs a companion change.",
