      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9102](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9102) at head `7a804e8d`.\n\nThe change filters `validity_map` keys with `if int(k)` so netuid **0** is omitted from the shared universe list, which matches how scoring and receipts already treat root (`int(n) > 0` in `snapshot_coverage`).\n\n**Main issue:** **`_shrink_allowed` blocks publishing** when an existing LKG still has `0` in `netuids` but the new build omits `0` without drop evidence—root is never eligible for removal, so `refresh_once` keeps the prior snapshot and the filter may never reach disk/API for those deployments.\n\n**Suggested follow-up:** exempt `ROOT_NETUID` from the shrink check, or normalize `0` out of prior membership when building, so the placeholder skip can actually land.\n\nDeclared blocking tag: `poisons-later-row`. Gate fixture still shows `next: review`; formal verdict was recorded via `post_verdict`.",
