            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001` replaces the owner rule in `_merge_sources` for TaoMarketCap-listed netuids that the chain definitively excludes. That contradicts the pinned membership contract for this review and re-opens a path where deregistered netuids never leave the shared universe.\n\n## Measured\n\n- `get_pr_diff` / `read_repo_file` at head: the removed branch returned `\"negative\"`, started or kept `negative_since`, and treated TMC+chain disagreement as chain-wins when `probe_positive is False` and `tmc_positive is not False`.\n- The new branch runs when `tmc_positive is True and probe_positive is False` and returns `\"positive\"` with `disputed=True`, `negative_since=None`, and `refresh_incomplete=False`.\n- `_default_probe_fetch` (head) only emits `probe_positive is False` after `outcome == \"ok\"`, a pinned finalized head, and a complete membership read; failed/timeout/incomplete reads return `{}` with `complete=False`, leaving probe unobserved (`None`), not False.\n- Removal still requires `validity == \"negative\"` and `_eligible_for_removal` (probe `False`, `negative_since` set, 48h grace). Disputed `\"positive\"` rows never enter that path.\n- `_compute_membership` still iterates prior members in `candidates`, so a prior member kept as disputed-positive remains in `validity_map` and published snapshot rows.\n\n## Inferred\n\nWhen TMC still lists a netuid the chain no longer registers, the head keeps it in `/api/subnets` and pump membership indefinitely (disputed but positive), instead of starting the grace clock toward removal. That is the opposite of “definitive chain negative beats TaoMarketCap listing.”\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Severity | Label |\n|----|----------|-------|\n| F1 | P1 | **measured** Contract violation: definitive chain negative + TMC listing no longer drives `\"negative\"` / grace; subnet stays positive. |\n| F2 | P1 | **inferred** Rows that should expire after chain deregistration can **never-expires** under persistent TMC ghost listings (no `negative_since`, not eligible for drop). |\n\n## Recommendation\n\nRestore chain-wins behavior for `probe_positive is False` with a complete probe (including when `tmc_positive is True`), or narrow the new dispute branch so it cannot apply to a definitive chain negative. Optionally surface `disputed=True` without overriding validity to positive.\n\nBlocking: F2 (`never-expires`).",
