      "finalText": "**FAIL** at head `1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001` — formal comment posted via `post_verdict`.\n\n### What changed\nThe PR replaces the old `_merge_sources` rule (“complete chain read that omits the netuid → `negative` and grace, chain wins over TMC”) with a branch that, when **TMC lists the netuid** and **probe is definitively false**, returns **`positive` + `disputed=True`** and clears `negative_since`.\n\n### Why this fails review\n**Measured:** `_default_probe_fetch` only sets `probe_positive is False` after a successful, complete registration read (`outcome == \"ok\"`). Failed, timed-out, or incomplete reads leave probe unobserved (`None`), not false — matching your pinned contract.\n\n**Measured:** Removal still requires `validity == \"negative\"`, `probe is False`, and 48h from `negative_since`. Disputed **positive** rows never enter that path.\n\n**Inferred:** A netuid deregistered on chain but still on TMC can stay in the shared universe forever (disputed but positive), which violates “definitive chain negative beats TaoMarketCap listing” and is declared blocking as **`never-expires`**.\n\n### Skills\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_merge_sources` → removal/shrink gates | — |\n| owner-rules | Removed “chain wins” behavior for TMC+probe disagree | — |\n| settled-check | Base already encoded chain-wins; no settled override in fixture | — |\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post; one MC verdict was posted for this head. Joshua owns any follow-up fix on the branch.",
