            "body": "## Summary\n\nRemoves the `is_universe_refresh_writer()` early return at the top of `refresh_once`, so non-worker callers run the full TMC + chain probe build and `_publish` instead of only `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`. That matches the PR goal (**inferred** from title): web (or any process) that invokes `refresh_once` can refresh membership instead of being redirected to a disk reload that never runs when no worker updates the file.\n\n## Blocking — shared persist / stale prior (**inferred**)\n\n`refresh_once` still does `build = self._builder.build(self._snapshot)` with no prior `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (**measured** at head). `_snapshot` is process-local; `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` is what picks up a newer `subnet_universe.json` from another VM (**measured**).\n\nIn split web + worker (or multi-web) with a shared `DATA_DIR`, **inferred** failure mode:\n\n1. Worker refreshes and `_atomic_persist`s a newer snapshot.\n2. Web still holds an older in-memory `_snapshot` (nothing forced a reload before this call).\n3. Web `refresh_once` builds from that stale prior and `_publish` overwrites the on-disk file.\n\nDownstream readers then load a persisted `validity_map` / membership rooted in stale prior state (grace clocks, shrink evidence, negative_since). That fits **poisons-later-row** on the shared persistence seam.\n\nThe removed guard used to avoid full publish on non-writers; opening refresh without **reload-before-build** (or a cross-process refresh lock) trades one stale-web symptom for a clobber risk.\n\n## Non-blocking notes (**inferred** / **measured**)\n\n- `is_universe_refresh_writer()` docstring still says only workers may refresh/publish (**measured**), but `refresh_once` no longer enforces that; `kick_refresh_async` / `ensure_refresh_loop` still gate on the helper (**measured**). Docs and entry paths should stay aligned.\n- `_refresh_lock` is process-local only (**measured**); concurrent refreshes across processes are not serialized.\n- Shrink / LKG / emergency retention inside `refresh_once` unchanged (**measured**); no new float/`1e308` path in this diff.\n\n## Suggested fix (**inferred**)\n\nAt the start of `refresh_once` (before `build`), call `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` so `self._snapshot` reflects the latest shared persist when mtime is newer, then run the build; or use an explicit cross-process lock around refresh+persist.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Stale prior → persist overwrite on shared file | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins / 48h grace logic unchanged in diff; split-mode writer semantics now inconsistent with docs | — |\n| settled-check | No fixture docs/locks to re-litigate split refresh ownership | — |",
