            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line guard change in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: drop `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` so hot reload defers to `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` after an `isinstance(payload, dict)` check.\n\n## Adversarial trace (real entry: `ensure_universe_reader` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale`)\n\n**Measured:** At head, the reload path reads JSON, requires a dict, calls `from_dict`, and on any exception logs and returns the prior in-memory `_snapshot` without updating `_disk_mtime`.\n\n**Measured:** `from_dict` builds `netuids` via `tuple(sorted(int(n) for n in payload.get(\"netuids\") or []))`; missing or empty `netuids` yields an empty tuple, not an exception.\n\n**Measured (base):** The removed guard treated falsy `netuids` (missing key or `[]`) as “do not reload”, so web readers could keep a stale in-memory universe while the worker had already atomically persisted a newer **degraded empty** build (`netuids=tuple()` from `SnapshotBuilder` when membership resolves empty).\n\n**Inferred:** That stale-reader behavior is the regression this PR fixes; accepting well-formed dicts with empty `netuids` matches worker-published state and aligns with `get_lkg_or_emergency()` still substituting `emergency_registry` when `not snap.netuids` on the LKG API path.\n\n**Inferred:** `get_snapshot()` / pump rows can reflect an empty persisted universe after reload; council admission remains fail-closed via `membership_allows_admission` when `degraded` or `refresh_incomplete` is set on the receipt (**measured** fields on persisted snapshots from builder paths).\n\n**Inferred:** Extreme values in `netuids` that make `int(n)` raise still abort the reload attempt and retain prior snapshot (**measured** try/except); no new overflow path in this diff.\n\n## Note (non-blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` truthy on process boot, while hot reload no longer does. **Inferred:** intentional conservatism at cold start vs picking up worker publishes after mtime bump; not introduced by this hunk.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nNo finding that rows never expire, overflow to inf/NaN, abort a refresh cycle, or persist poisoned state that a later cycle reads back beyond pre-existing `from_dict` tolerance. Change is minimal and targeted.\n\n| Severity | Finding |\n| --- | --- |\n| — | None blocking |",
