            "body": "## SimiBot comment → counted head (trace)\n\n**Measured** on `review-gate-bot/bot/lib/verdicts.ts` at head `2dee2723…`:\n\n1. `simibotMcHead(comment)` runs only when `user.login === simibot[bot]` and `performedViaGithubApp.id === 5501340` (**measured**: constants in file).\n2. It collects matches of `<!-- mc-verdict:([0-9a-f]{40}) -->`; exactly one match yields that 40-char string, otherwise the SimiBot MC path is skipped (**measured**).\n3. On that branch, `verdictFromComment` → `parseVerdictToken` → for `PASS`, `passTailAllowed(tail)` must return true (**measured**).\n4. If a verdict token is parsed, `collectPinnedVerdicts` pushes `{ reviewer: \"mc\", verdict, headSha: simibotHead, … }` — **`headSha` is always the marker SHA**, not anything read from the PASS tail (**measured**).\n\nSo a SimiBot comment that survives steps 1–3 is counted **for the head named in `mc-verdict`**, regardless of whether the first-line pointer agrees.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — PASS pointer vs `mc-verdict` marker not checked (SimiBot path)\n\n**Inferred** from control flow: when the first line includes a head pointer (`at …`, `head …`, bare SHA, etc.) that **does not** equal the marker head (including after resolving a ≥12-hex prefix via `resolveSha`), the pinned rule for this round requires **fail closed** (no MC verdict). The SimiBot branch never extracts the tail pointer, never calls `resolveSha`, and never compares to `simibotHead`; it still emits an MC verdict pinned to the marker.\n\n### P2 — Bare `PASS` with empty tail still parses\n\n**Inferred**: `passTailAllowed(\"\")` leaves `words` empty and returns `i === words.length` (true), so a first line of only `PASS` is accepted. That contradicts the PR title (“a PASS counts only with a head pointer **or** signature after it”) and leaves SimiBot comments that have a marker but no tail constraint able to count.\n\n### P3 — PASS tail accepts 7–11 hex “SHAs”\n\n**Measured**: `SHA_WORD = /^[0-9a-f]{7,40}$/i` in `passTailAllowed`. **Inferred**: the same module documents a **12**-character minimum for abbreviated head claims in `shaClaimedByComment` (comment block ~lines 318–325). The pinned rule for this review (≥12-hex prefix that **resolves** to the head) is not applied on the PASS first line.\n\n## What improved (measured)\n\nReplacing the `WITHDRAWN` regex with `passTailAllowed` correctly rejects many caveat tails (e.g. extra prose after `PASS`) that the old negation list missed.\n\nAdding the dedicated SimiBot branch correctly reads `<!-- mc-verdict:… -->` (distinct from `subnet-review-gate:mc-verdict:…`) and pins MC to that marker when author checks pass.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**MODIFY** — wire PASS-tail pointer extraction + `resolveSha` + equality check against `simibotHead` (reject entire SimiBot MC comment on mismatch); require non-empty tail to be pointer and/or signature only; align short-pointer minimum with the 12-hex claim rule (or document an intentional difference).",
