      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** at `2dee2723c015ef610ce36da8c0afdb37aed61c0a` on PR 1522.\n\nThe swap from the withdrawal regex to an allowlist (`passTailAllowed`) is the right move: extra words after `PASS` (caveats, notes) no longer parse as a verdict, and the SimiBot `<!-- mc-verdict:… -->` path ties MC to the marker head with `noteUnparsed` when the first line fails.\n\nAgainst **this round’s pinned pointer rule**, the head still falls short (**measured** / **inferred** as labeled in the PR comment):\n\n| Author-realistic first line | Expected | At this head |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PASS` (no pointer) | no PASS | still parses (**inferred**: empty `words` → `i === words.length`) |\n| `PASS deadbeef` / `PASS effaced` | no PASS | still parses (**inferred**: `SHA_WORD` allows 7–40 hex) |\n| `PASS` + 7–11 hex bare | no PASS | still parses |\n| `PASS` + ≥12 hex bare or full 40 | PASS if resolves | shape OK; resolution not checked in `passTailAllowed` (**measured**) |\n| `PASS -simibot` only | no PASS | still parses (**inferred**) |\n| `PASS deadbeef/effaced` | no PASS | rejected (**inferred**: slash token fails `SHA_WORD`) |\n\nMain fix: align the PASS tail with the same 12-character abbreviated rule already documented for `shaClaimedByComment`—bare pointer only at 40 chars, 12–39 only after `at` / `at head` / `head` / `on`, require a real pointer before an optional signature, and add tests for the pinned examples.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `parseVerdictToken` → `passTailAllowed`; walked pinned word cases through the splitter | — |\n| owner-rules | Fail-closed gate parsing; 12-char consistency with claim patterns in-file | — |\n| settled-check | Judged against this round’s pinned rule (no prior lock in fixture) | — |\n\nGate state still shows `next: review` in the fixture; MC verdict was posted via `post_verdict`.",
