otype.replace` cost for that scale is **well under 50 ms** on modern hardware.\n- **Guess:** Budget (2) is met, but this is not **measured** in MC.\n\n#### Budget checklist (pinned input)\n\n| Part | Old pattern | New pattern |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| (1) time(2N) ≤ 3× time(N) | **Inferred: fail** (quadratic) | **Inferred: pass** (~linear) |\n| (2) 200k chars ≤ 50 ms | **Inferred: fail** (often seconds on quadratic ReDoS shapes) | **Inferred: pass**; **guess** confirms pending author/CI timing |\n\nReal JWTs remain covered: three dot-separated segments of 8–2048 URL-safe characters is far above valid token sizes; comment in diff states intent.\n\n### Other diff hunks (assignment scrub, URL userinfo lookbehind)\n\n- **Inferred:** `scrubAssignments` traces from production entry `redactSecrets` → left-to-right `ASSIGNMENT_NAME` / `ASSIGNED_VALUE` with credential filter; non-credential assignments advance `lastIndex` via `RegExp.prototype.exec`, avoiding the infinite-loop shape on `continue` when the label is not a credential name.\n- **Inferred:** Nested `password=` inside a larger value is reachable because non-credential matches do not consume the remainder of the string—addresses the hole described in the new comment.\n- No **measured** path found for overflow / cycle-abort / row-poison semantics (N/A to this bot scrubber).\n\n### Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | JWT ReDoS on dotless `eyJ-` run; assignment scan entry point | — |\n| owner-rules | Bounded scrub time aligns with publishing-safe bot output | — |\n| settled-check | Quadratic JWT scrub called out in diff comment; bounded segments are the agreed fix direction | — |\n\n**Verdict:** The JWT change removes the unbounded quantifier that caused quadratic behavior on the pinned input. **Inferred** scaling meets (1); **inferred/guess** meets (2). Recommend a checked-in micro-bench (N vs 2N + 200k/50ms) when a runner is available so (2) is **measured**, not only in