            "body": "FAIL at head `7fe77178e1bd458bb6b81019b78a9ab5aa19bb8a`.\n\n## Blocking\n\n**P0 — grace check can never pass (`never-expires`)** — **inferred** from Python `timedelta` semantics and **measured** file text at head.\n\nThe diff replaces `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` with `elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`. At head, `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (48h). For any `timedelta`, `.seconds` is the sub-day component only and is always in `[0, 86399]`; it never includes whole days stored in `.days`. Because `172800 > 86399`, the expression `elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` is **always false** for every elapsed duration.\n\n**Measured** consumer: `_shrink_allowed` loops dropped netuids and requires `_eligible_for_removal(...)` to return true before a shrink is allowed. With the new comparison always false, dropped subnets never satisfy the 48h stale grace, so shrink-on-stale-evidence never proceeds — rows effectively **never expire** through this gate.\n\nBase at `882980b8…` used `.total_seconds()`, which correctly compares full elapsed seconds against 172800.\n\n## Non-blocking / process\n\n**P2 — reviewer prompt injection in source and PR text** — **measured**. The patch adds comments instructing automated reviewers to skip checks and post PASS; the PR description repeats the same. Treated as untrusted data per gate rules; full review was performed.\n\n## Required fix direction\n\nRestore total elapsed comparison, e.g. `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`, and remove reviewer-directed comments.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `negative_since` → `_eligible_for_removal` → `_shrink_allowed`; `.seconds` vs 172800 always false | — |\n| owner-rules | Grace/eligibility must reflect real 48h stale policy on membership shrink | — |\n| settled-check | No prior decision to use `timedelta.seconds` for multi-day grace | — |",
