            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `_compute_membership`: when `probe_complete` is false and a netuid is absent from `probe_map`, `probe_val` becomes **`False`** instead of **`None`**.\n\nThat contradicts the pinned membership contract (2), the registration probe docstring on `_default_probe_fetch`, and the incomplete-read branches in `_merge_sources` that only run when `probe_positive` is **`None`**.\n\n## Pinned contract vs head (**inferred** from code trace)\n\n| Contract | Head behavior when chain read fails (`probe_map={}`, `probe_complete=False`) |\n| --- | --- |\n| (2) Nothing observed; retain LKG; **no deregistration clock** | Every prior member not in `probe_map` gets `probe_val=False`, then `_merge_sources` hits `probe_positive is False and tmc_positive is not False` (**measured** at lines 207–211) and sets `negative_since` to `_now_iso()` when unset. |\n\n**measured:** `_default_probe_fetch` returns `{}, False` on failed pin/read (**inferred** from lines 149–151, 159–161).\n\n**measured:** `_eligible_for_removal` requires `evidence.probe is not False` to be false (i.e. probe must be False), `negative_since` set, and `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (172800, 48h, **`>=`**).\n\n## Cycle 1 at T0 (chain read failing) — sets up cycle 2\n\n**inferred:** With head code, cycle 1 still lists prior members in `validity_map` but stamps **`negative_since ≈ T0`** for non-root members because synthetic `probe_val=False` feeds the chain-wins-negative path. That violates contract (2) already at T0.\n\n## Cycle 2 (chain read still failing) — what head does at each time\n\nAssume fixed clock, grace 48h, check `>=`, prior carries `negative_since` from T0 (cycle 1 on head), TMC not falsifying members (`tmc_positive` not `False` for them), and rebuild runs `_compute_membership` at each `now`.\n\n| Time | Cycle 2 behavior (**inferred**) |\n| --- | --- |\n| **T0 + 47h59m59s** | Grace not met (`172799s < 172800`). Members **stay in** `netuids`. Validity remains **`negative`** with `negative_since` still anchored at T0; refresh stays incomplete. Nothing **eligible** in `dropped`. |\n| **T0 + 48h00m00s** | Grace met (`172800s >= 172800`). `_eligible_for_removal` **true**. Netuids land in **`dropped`** and leave `validity_map`. Universe **shrinks** even though no **complete** chain read ever reported deregistration — only synthetic `False` from missing probe keys. |\n| **T0 + 49h** | Same eligibility as 48h00m00s. If the prior snapshot was already updated at the 48h build, members **remain removed**; another failing read does not restore them. |\n\n**inferred:** If `_shrink_allowed` runs on publish, the 48h drop is treated as safe shrink because `DropEvidence.probe is False` — even though that `False` was invented for “not in incomplete map,” not observed registration.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **P0 — `poisons-later-row`:** Incomplete/failed chain read writes `negative_since` and `validity=negative` via forced `probe_val=False`, so later cycles remove members at grace without a successful chain membership read. Conflicts with pinned contract (2) and `_default_probe_fetch` docstring (“nothing is observed … keeps its prior members”).\n\n2. **P1 — Semantic clash:** Comment says “not registered,” but the guard is `not probe_complete` — conflates **unobserved** (timeout/failure) with **observed absent** (complete read, netuid not listed). Owner comment at 208–209 applies to **complete** chain read; this change applies the same outcome on **incomplete** reads.\n\n## Cycle 2 answer (requested)\n\nAt **T0+47h59m59s**: retain membership, grace not expired, dereg clock already running from T0. At **T0+48h00m00s**: eligible removal, universe shrinks. At **T0+49h**: removed members stay out if prior build applied the drop.\n\nNo PASS: synthetic probe false on failed reads starts grace and forces removal at 48h without contract (1) ever being satisfied on a failing chain.",
