      "finalText": "**Verdict:** **FAIL** posted on PR 9306 at `7b1b568539ffbaaf49ccc7a4d14ff1bcceff79c5` (blocking: `poisons-later-row`).\n\n### What the change does\n\nWhen the chain read fails or times out, `probe_map` is empty and `probe_complete` is false. **Head** sets `probe_val = False` for every netuid not in the map (instead of **`None`**). That feeds `_merge_sources` the “chain says not registered” path (`probe_positive is False` and `tmc_positive is not False`), which **starts or keeps `negative_since`** even though `_default_probe_fetch` documents that a failed read means **nothing observed** and prior members should be kept **without** a deregistration clock. That conflicts with your pinned contract (2).\n\n### Cycle 2 at the three times (**inferred**, assuming cycle 1 at T0 on the same head already set `negative_since ≈ T0` while the chain read kept failing)\n\n| Time | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| **T0 + 47h59m59s** | Grace not satisfied (`47h59m59s < 48h`). Members **remain** in the universe. Validity stays **negative** with the clock anchored at T0; nothing is **eligible** for removal yet. |\n| **T0 + 48h00m00s** | Grace satisfied (`>= 172800`). Members become **eligible**, land in **`dropped`**, and **leave** `netuids` — a shrink **without** any complete successful chain membership read. |\n| **T0 + 49h** | Same eligibility as at 48h; if the 48h build was applied, removed netuids **stay out**; another failing read does not bring them back. |\n\nSo under head code, a **still-failing** chain read does **not** honor “retain LKG, no dereg clock”; it eventually **drops** members at the 48h boundary off synthetic `probe=False`, not off contract (1).\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review`; the formal **FAIL** was posted via `post_verdict`. I cannot merge or change the PR from here — that stays with Joshua if you want a fix (revert to `probe_val = None` on incomplete reads, or only treat absence as false when `probe_complete` is true).",
