      "finalText": "## Review (head `10bfa73cdbee1025a1466d6247d879ebe3d6b56e`)\n\n**Measured:** `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (48h). The diff replaces `total_seconds()` with `timedelta.seconds` in `_eligible_for_removal`.\n\n**Inferred:** For a deregistered netuid (`probe is False`, valid `negative_since`), eligibility is that comparison only (other guards pass).\n\n### What the comparison does at concrete elapsed times\n\n| Elapsed | Base: `total_seconds() >= 172800` | Head: `elapsed.seconds >= 172800` |\n|--------|-------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|\n| **23h** | False (still in grace) | False (`seconds` = 82 800) |\n| **24h** | False (86 400 < 172 800) | False (`days`=1 → **`seconds`=0**, not 86 400) |\n| **25h** | False | False (`seconds`=3 600) |\n| **47h59m** | False | False (`seconds`=86 340) |\n| **48h** | **True** (grace met) | **False** (`days`=2 → **`seconds`=0**) |\n| **49h** | True | False (`seconds`=3 600) |\n\nPast 24h elapsed, the head code stops measuring wall-clock age in `seconds`: whole days sit in `elapsed.days`, so `elapsed.seconds` is only the remainder within the current day (0–86 399). It **never** reaches 172 800, so removal eligibility never turns on after grace—**`never-expires`** for shrink (`_shrink_allowed` / stale members).\n\n**Verdict:** **FAIL** posted via `post_verdict` with blocking `never-expires`. Restore `elapsed.total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (or an equivalent timedelta compare).",
