            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `_compute_membership`: build `netuids` from `validity_map` keys with `if int(k)`, skipping falsy netuid **0** while leaving the root validity entry in `validity_map`.\n\n## Trace (real entry point)\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` → `get_netuids()` / `get_pump_membership_rows()` / `load_membership_receipt()` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`, `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`).\n\n**Measured:** Keys written into `validity_map` in this function are only `str(netuid)` for `netuid in sorted(candidates)`; candidates are ints from TMC/probe/prior membership, plus `ROOT_NETUID` (0) when `observed_members` is non-empty.\n\n**Inferred:** Before this head, a non-empty refresh with only the root slot in the map could yield `netuids == [0]`, which `_build_rows` would turn into a synthetic row for netuid 0. Downstream already treats root as non-membership (`membership_scoring_expected` and receipt netuid lists use `int(n) > 0`; receipt exposes `root_netuid_in_membership`). This diff aligns the published membership list with that policy.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n| Input | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| Key `\"0\"` | Skipped from `netuids` (**measured** intent of diff). |\n| Keys `\"1\"`…`\"199\"` | Included unchanged. |\n| `1e308`, `NaN`, bad strings as map keys | **Inferred:** Not produced by this loop; malformed persisted `validity_map` keys are not re-keyed here—only candidate netuids get entries each cycle. No new abort path in the comprehension beyond existing `int(k)` on digit keys. |\n| Overflow to `inf` | N/A (integer netuid keys only). |\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured:** Merge/grace/chain-wins logic in `_merge_sources` untouched. Excluding 0 from membership matches existing scoring/coverage rules (root never scored; emergency registry already skips netuid 0).\n\n## Settled\n\n**Inferred:** Partial mitigation already existed at receipt/scoring layers