            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis head replaces the early `_merge_sources` branch that applied a **definitive chain negative** (`probe_positive is False` with `tmc_positive is not False`) with a narrower branch that only fires when **both** `tmc_positive is True` and `probe_positive is False`, returning **`positive` + `disputed`** instead of **`negative` + `negative_since`**.\n\nThat contradicts the pinned membership contract for this review (**measured**: user pin) and the owner rule that was documented on the removed base branch (**measured**: base diff comment).\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1 — Chain negative no longer beats TMC listing (blocking)\n\n**Measured** (head `internal/subnet_universe.py`): when `tmc_positive is True` and `probe_positive is False`, the function returns `\"positive\"`, `disputed=True`, `negative_since=None`.\n\n**Measured** (base via diff): the same signal pair previously returned `\"negative\"`, set `negative_since`, and treated TMC listing as disputed only (`tmc_positive is True` on disputed flag) while still starting the removal grace clock.\n\n**Inferred** (entry `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources`): a complete registration probe with `probe_map[netuid]=False` means the netuid was absent from `get_member_netuids` at a pinned finalized head (**measured**: probe fetch builds `observed[n] = n in registered` only after `outcome == \"ok\"`). That is a definitive chain negative, not a timeout/unknown.\n\n**Inferred**: with this change, such a netuid remains in `validity_map` as **positive** and never accumulates `negative_since`, so `_eligible_for_removal` never runs on that evidence path and the subnet stays in `snap.netuids` / `expected_netuids` despite chain exclusion.\n\n**Measured** (`internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` `load_membership_receipt`): only `validity == \"negative\"` netuids become `inactive_netuids`; positive/disputed rows stay in `expected_netuids`.\n\nPinned contract: definitive chain negative beats TaoMarketCap listing — **violated**.\n\n### F2 — `probe False` + incomplete TMC no longer forces negative (blocking)\n\n**Measured**: removing `probe_positive is False and tmc_positive is not False` drops handling for `probe False` + `tmc None` (and other non-False TMC states except explicit `True`, which now goes to dispute-positive).\n\n**Inferred**: those cases fall through to `tmc_positive is None or probe_positive is None`, which preserves prior **positive/unobserved** validity with `refresh_incomplete` instead of starting `negative_since`. That treats a **complete** probe negative like an unknown read for membership verdict purposes.\n\nPinned contract: failed/timeout/unknown chain read is NOT a negative — **OK**; complete probe negative **should** still negative — **broken** for `tmc None`.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `probe False` + `tmc True/None` through `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources` → receipt inactive set | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins-over-TMC rule removed/inverted on disagreement | — |\n| settled-check | Pin matches prior in-code owner comment on base branch; not a settled dispute outcome | — |\n\n## Verdict\n\n**FAIL** — do not merge until definitive chain negatives again set `negative` + grace (and TMC-only disagreement does not keep subnets in `expected_netuids`).\n",
