      "finalText": "## Verdict: **FAIL** (posted on PR 9103 @ `1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001`)\n\nThis change swaps the old “chain wins” branch for a TMC-vs-probe **dispute → stay positive** path. That conflicts with your pinned rule: a **complete** chain read that omits the netuid must beat a TaoMarketCap listing; only failed/timeout/unknown reads are non-negatives.\n\n**What the diff does (measured):** For `tmc_positive is True` and `probe_positive is False`, head returns `validity=\"positive\"`, `disputed=True`, and `negative_since=None`. Base returned `validity=\"negative\"`, started the grace clock, and only flagged dispute when TMC also listed the netuid.\n\n**Why that is blocking (inferred from head code):** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources` → `load_membership_receipt` only treats `validity == \"negative\"` as inactive. Definitive `probe False` (probe completes with `outcome == \"ok\"`) no longer drives negative/grace on the TMC-listed disagreement path, so those netuids can remain in `expected_netuids` indefinitely (`never-expires`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\n**Secondary regression (inferred):** Dropping `probe_positive is False and tmc_positive is not False` also removes immediate negative handling for `probe False` + `tmc None`; those cases fall into the incomplete-read preserve-prior path instead of a chain negative.\n\nRestore chain-wins for any definitive `probe False` (including vs TMC `True`), keep dispute as metadata on a **negative** row if you want it visible, and only skip negative when the probe is incomplete/unknown—not when it successfully excludes the netuid.",
