          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `b82cb42ad571e30d7ba9ae2cc97df36fd299a25c` adds TMC-related **environment values** to the warning emitted when `_default_tmc_fetch()` fails. That is a secret-leak regression, not a safe diagnostics improvement.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P0 — TMC API key (and other secrets) written to application logs\n\n**measured:** The diff at `internal/subnet_universe.py` builds `tmc_env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k.upper().startswith((\"TMC\", \"TAOMARKETCAP\"))}` and passes it to `logger.warning(..., tmc_env)` on any exception from `_get_all_subnets_tao()`.\n\n**measured:** The author’s staging excerpt shows the new format: upstream 502 plus a `config:` dict that includes `TMC_API_KEY` with the **full secret value** (not redacted).\n\n**inferred:** Warning logs on staging/production typically land in centralized retention (CloudWatch, etc.), so every TMC fetch failure (502, timeout, auth errors) **re-publishes** credentials to durable stores and to anyone with log read access.\n\n**inferred:** Entry path is production refresh: `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once()` → `SnapshotBuilder.build()` → `_default_tmc_fetch()`; behavior on failure remains `tmc_complete=False` and prior universe retention — unchanged from base — but the new log line is additional harmful side effect.\n\n**Required fix:** Do not log secret **values**. If config hints are needed on failure, log only variable **names**, or booleans like `TMC_API_KEY=set|unset`, or a redaction helper that masks `*_KEY`, `*_SECRET`, `*_TOKEN` values. Revert the raw env dict dump.\n\n**Operational note:** Because staging already emitted the key in this format, **rotate `TMC_API_KEY`** (and audit log sinks) — name the variable only; do not paste values in PR comments.\n\n## Not in scope for blocking gate tags\n\nNo new path for `never-expires`, float overflow, cycle abort, or cross-row poison in universe membership math — failure handling still returns incomplete TMC and holds prior snapshot (**inferred** from unchanged control flow after the `except` block).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_default_tmc_fetch` through refresh loop; confirmed new log is the only functional addition on the exception path | — |\n| owner-rules | Standing rule: never print secret values in logs or reviews — this diff prints `TMC_API_KEY` value on every fetch failure | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in fixture repo endorsing full TMC env dumps; prior base logged `%s` for `exc` only (**measured** base lines 127–128) | — |",
            "headSha": "b82cb42ad571e30d7ba9ae2cc97df36fd299a25c",
