      "finalText": "**FAIL** posted on PR 9105 at head `b82cb42ad571e30d7ba9ae2cc97df36fd299a25c`.\n\nThe change builds a dict of every `TMC*` / `TAOMARKETCAP*` environment variable **with values** and logs it on any TMC fetch exception. Your staging line is exactly what the diff does: the warning includes `TMC_API_KEY` in plaintext. **measured** from the patch and your log; **inferred** that each 502/timeout/auth failure copies credentials into log retention.\n\nUniverse behavior on failure is unchanged (still `tmc_complete=False`, hold prior membership). The problem is purely credential exposure.\n\n**Fix:** log only names, or `set`/`unset`, or redact `*_KEY` / `*_SECRET` / `*_TOKEN` — never raw env values. Because staging already logged the key in this format, rotate `TMC_API_KEY` and review log access (variable name only; do not paste the value in the PR).",
