            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: drop `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` so any JSON object dict is passed to `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`, matching the PR title (reload well-formed persisted snapshots, including legitimately empty `netuids`).\n\n## Entry point traced\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_universe_reader()` → `get_provider().reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (web/read-only path). On stale mtime, the method loads JSON, requires `isinstance(payload, dict)`, builds via `from_dict`, and on any exception logs and retains the in-memory snapshot.\n\n**Measured:** `from_dict` normalizes `netuids` with `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []`, coercing each element with `int(n)` inside a sorted tuple comprehension; non-coercible values raise and hit the existing `except` path (no swap-in).\n\n**Inferred:** Previously, a worker-persisted snapshot with `netuids: []` (e.g. degraded empty membership from `SnapshotBuilder`) was ignored on reload because `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` is true for `[]`; the reader could stay pinned to an older, larger in-memory universe. After this change, the reader adopts the on-disk snapshot, which is the intended cross-process sync behavior.\n\n## Extremes / poison checks\n\n| Input | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `{}` | **Inferred:** `netuids=()`, default `status=\"ok\"`; `load_membership_receipt` → `fresh=False` when `resolved_at` missing; `membership_allows_admission` fail-closed. |\n| `netuids: []` with `status: \"degraded\"` | **Measured:** Persisted shape from builder; admission blocked via `degraded` / `refresh_incomplete` flags in `membership_allows_admission`. |\n| `get_lkg_or_emergency()` | **Measured:** `not snap.netuids` → `emergency_registry(reason=\"no_usable_snapshot\")` for API paths that use the emergency seam. |\n| `1e308`, `inf`, bad strings in `netuids` | **Inferred:** `int(n)` or JSON load failures → exception path; snapshot unchanged. |\n\nNo path found where this diff alone makes grace rows never expire, overflows to `inf`/`NaN` in membership math, aborts a refresh cycle uncaught, or writes unbounded bad state that a later cycle reads without the existing guards (`_shrink_allowed`, `_hold_prior`, admission gating).\n\n## Non-blocking note (P3)\n\n**Inferred:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` on cold start, while hot reload no longer does. Asymmetric but out of this diff’s scope; optional follow-up for consistency.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured:** Comments and `snapshot_coverage` continue to treat stale/degraded/emergency membership as fail-closed for scoring; aligning reader reload with worker-published empty/degraded snapshots does not weaken chain-wins or 48h-grace logic in `_compute_membership`.\n\n## Settled\n\n**Guess:** No roadmap/docs in this fixture slice; nothing contradicts adopting persisted worker snapshots on the reader path.",
