            "body": "PASS\n\n## JWT pattern (`VALUE_PATTERNS`, head)\n\nPattern under review:\n`/(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\\b/g`\n\nReplaces base `/\\beyJ…{8,}\\.…{8,}\\.…{8,}\\b/g`, which the diff comment correctly identifies as quadratic on long `eyJ` runs **without** dots (each anchor rescans an unbounded tail looking for `.`).\n\n### Budget (1): N vs 2N wall time\n\n**inferred** (algorithm on the pinned pattern; this session has no shell/Node runner—timing was not **measured** here):\n\n- Input family: `(\"eyJ-\").repeat(k)` → length `4k`, no dots.\n- `(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])eyJ` fires at roughly one anchor every four characters → **Θ(k) anchors**.\n- After each `eyJ`, the first segment is `{8,2048}` then a required `.`. With no dot in the string, the engine tries a **bounded** backtrack (at most ~2048−8 steps on the first segment) and moves on.\n- Total work **Θ(k · 2048) = Θ(n)** in input length `n = 4k`.\n- Doubling input length doubles anchor count with a constant cap per anchor → expected wall-time ratio **≈2×**, comfortably within the **≤3×** gate.\n\nBase pattern on the same input: unbounded `{8,}` on the first segment → **Θ(n²)** (**inferred**); that is what this PR fixes.\n\n### Budget (2): 200 000 characters (`eyJ-` × 50 000)\n\n**inferred** work ≈ 50 000 anchors × O(2048) first-segment trials ≈ **10⁸** engine steps (order-of-magnitude). That is linear in `n` with a fixed segment cap, not a nested rescan of the tail. On typical V8 builds this class of bounded-failure JWT scrub is expected to land **well under 50 ms** (**guess**: low tens of ms worst case; not **measured** in this environment).\n\n| Criterion | Meets budget? | Basis |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2N ≤ 3× N time | Yes | **inferred** Θ(n) |\n| 200k chars ≤ 50 ms | Yes (expected) | **inferred** + **guess**; confirm in CI/Node locally |\n\nReal JWTs still match (segments ≪ 2048). A hypothetical token with a segment **>2048** would not match and could leak (**inferred**, P3; outside this round’s ReDoS budget).\n\n## Other diff hunks (brief)\n\n- **`scrubAssignments`**: **inferred** left-to-right scan; non-credential `name=` matches advance via `RegExp#exec`; credential values at EOF with no token do not spin (**inferred** trace of `lastIndex` after `names.exec`). Nested `password=` inside a quoted value remains reachable vs the monolithic `NAMED_ASSIGNMENT` replace (**inferred**, aligns with comment intent).\n- **`URL_USERINFO` lookbehind**: **inferred** tighter scheme boundary; not on the JWT budget path.\n\n## Severity\n\nNo P0/P1 blocking items for gate categories (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`). JWT ReDoS on scrub input was a cycle-stall risk on base; head bounds segment work (**inferred**).\n\nRecommend adding a committed micro-benchmark (N / 2N / 200k) next to `redact.ts` so CI records **measured** timings for this budget.",
