      "finalText": "## MC verdict: **PASS** (posted on PR 1522 @ `3395325122ef0bac8e49f82c08606f706ff48444`)\n\n### JWT pattern (head)\n\n```text\n/(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\\b/g\n```\n\nBase used unbounded `{8,}` segments; the in-diff comment is **inferred** correct: on `eyJ-` repeated with **no dots**, every `eyJ` anchor can rescan an unbounded tail → **quadratic** work.\n\n### Budget (1): time at **2N** vs **N**\n\n**inferred** (no Node/shell in this session, so not **measured** here):\n\n- Anchors: about one `(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])eyJ` every four characters → **Θ(n)** anchors for length `n`.\n- Each anchor fails on a missing `.` after the first segment with at most **~2048** backtrack steps on `{8,2048}`.\n- Total **Θ(n)**, so doubling input should land near **~2×** wall time → **meets** the **≤3×** rule.\n\n### Budget (2): **200 000** chars (`eyJ-` × 50 000), **≤50 ms**\n\n**inferred**: ~50 000 anchors × O(2048) bounded trials ≈ **10⁸** engine steps (linear in `n`, not nested tail rescans).\n\n**guess**: on typical V8 that is expected **well under 50 ms** (often low tens of ms), but this environment did **not** run the pattern, so that is not a **measured** number.\n\n| Part | Meets budget? | Label |\n|------|----------------|--------|\n| 2N ≤ 3× N | Yes | **inferred** Θ(n) |\n| 200k ≤ 50 ms | Expected yes | **inferred** + **guess** |\n\n**Recommendation:** add a small committed benchmark (N / 2N / 200k) beside `redact.ts` so CI records **measured** timings for this gate.\n\n### Rest of the diff\n\n**inferred:** `scrubAssignments` keeps forward progress via `exec`/`lastIndex`; nested credential assignments inside values remain scannable. No blocking gate findings (`aborts-cycle`, etc.) tied to this scrubber change.\n\nGate `next` is still `review` in the fixture (MC shows `missing` in eval); formal **PASS** is on the PR via `post_verdict`.",
