            "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds one `logger.info` after shrink is allowed and before `_publish`, listing netuids dropped from the prior snapshot versus the built snapshot.\n\n## Log line contents (can it carry a secret?)\n\n**Measured:** The format is `subnet_universe removed %d netuid(s) after the 48h grace: %s` with `len(removed)` and `removed`, where `removed = sorted(set(self._snapshot.netuids) - set(built.netuids))` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` at head). That expands to a decimal count and Python’s string form of a sorted list of integers taken from `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` (`Tuple[int, ...]`).\n\n**Inferred:** The line does not include registry rows, TMC payloads, env vars, tokens, or `persist_file` paths—only public subnet indices. It should not carry a secret unless some other layer misconfigured logging to exfiltrate unrelated fields (this call does not pass them).\n\n## How often it can fire\n\n**Measured:** The log runs only inside `refresh_once()` on the universe refresh writer path, after the emergency-retain and unsafe-shrink `_hold_prior` branches, and only when `removed` is non-empty. Blocked shrinks replace `built` with the prior universe, so `removed` is empty and this line does not run (the existing warning still logs `removed=` on block). Each qualifying refresh emits at most **one** info line aggregating every netuid dropped that cycle.\n\n**Measured:** Periodic refreshes use `REFRESH_INTERVAL_SECONDS = 300` in `_refresh_loop`; `kick_refresh_async` can trigger additional `refresh_once()` calls. **Inferred:** In steady state, at most about one such line per five minutes per worker unless an async kick coincides with an allowed shrink in the same cycle window.\n\n## Most netuids one line can list\n\n**Measured:** One line lists every member of `removed` for that publish; there is no chunking. The count is `len(prior.netuids) - len(built.netuids)` for that cycle.\n\n**Inferred:** Upper bound is all prior members minus those still in `built`. Root (`ROOT_NETUID = 0`) is never eligible for removal (`_eligible_for_removal`), so if root stays in `built` while every other member drops after grace, the list holds at most `len(self._snapshot.netuids) - 1` integers. If the prior snapshot had no root in `netuids`, the list could reach `len(self._snapshot.netuids)`. `MAX_NETUIDS = 200` bounds probe scan width, not a hard cap on persisted membership size, so very large on-disk universes could yield a long list in one line (operational noise, not a correctness bug).\n\n## Adversarial review\n\n**Measured:** Traced `refresh_once` → build → `_shrink_allowed` / `_hold_prior` → new log → `_publish`. No new accepted external input; no change to grace, shrink gate, or persistence. Logging cannot abort a cycle or poison a later row.\n\n## Owner rules / settled\n\n**Inferred:** Observability only; chain-wins and 48h grace semantics unchanged. No settled doc in fixture to contradict.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Confirmed log only on allowed shrink publish; ints-only payload | — |\n| owner-rules | No membership/grace behavior change | — |\n| settled-check | No prior decision in fixture blocks this log | — |",
