      "finalText": "**Verdict:** **PASS** posted for head `3d2338b70231def2b55252c1d130c3bec27b1ed8`.\n\n### What the new log line can contain (secrets?)\n\n**Measured:** After an allowed shrink, `refresh_once` logs:\n\n`subnet_universe removed %d netuid(s) after the 48h grace: %s`\n\nwith `len(removed)` and `removed`, where `removed = sorted(set(self._snapshot.netuids) - set(built.netuids))`. That is a count plus the usual string form of a **sorted list of integers** from the snapshot tuple.\n\n**Inferred:** No API keys, env, file paths, or full TMC/registry rows—only subnet netuids (public indices). This call should not emit secrets.\n\n### How often it can fire\n\n**Measured:** Only in `refresh_once` when `removed` is non-empty **after** emergency retain and unsafe-shrink `_hold_prior` (blocked shrinks leave `built` same size, so no info line). At most **one line per refresh** that actually publishes a smaller universe, listing every netuid dropped that cycle.\n\n**Measured:** The background loop sleeps `REFRESH_INTERVAL_SECONDS` (300s) between refreshes; `kick_refresh_async` can add extra `refresh_once` calls. **Inferred:** Roughly at most one such line every five minutes per worker in steady state, plus any kick-triggered cycles that coincide with an allowed shrink.\n\n### Most netuids one line can list\n\n**Measured:** The whole `removed` list in a single log record—no batching. Count equals netuids lost from prior to `built` that cycle.\n\n**Inferred:** At most `len(self._snapshot.netuids)` if every prior member drops; if root (0) stays in `built` while others age out, at most **`len(prior) - 1`** because root is never eligible for removal. `MAX_NETUIDS = 200` limits probe scan width, not necessarily persisted membership size, so a very large on-disk universe could produce a long one-line list (noise only, not a gate blocker).\n\nThe formal comment on the PR includes the skills table and adversarial trace. Gate fixture still shows `next: review` locally; down