      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted on head `4c4d504eee36e0617dca66ad590c94f8f8d90845`)\n\nReviewed the single-file diff in `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`. There is **no production code change**, so the adversarial pass did not surface any blocking paths (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\n### Why MODIFY, not PASS\n\n1. **`test_chain_never_removes_root_even_if_a_probe_reports_it_unregistered`** — **Measured:** the stub still reports `{0: False, 42: True}`, but the test now only does `assert built is not None`, so it no longer checks that netuid **0** stays in membership or stays non-`negative`. **Inferred:** `_compute_membership` still special-cases `ROOT_NETUID`, and `test_cold_start_keeps_root_when_chain_lists_1_to_128_and_tmc_is_incomplete` covers root elsewhere, but not this “probe says 0 unregistered” integration.\n\n2. **`test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing`** — **Measured:** the owner-rule docstring is unchanged, but `validity == \"negative\"`, `disputed`, and `negative_since` asserts were removed; only `42 in built.netuids` remains. **Measured:** overlapping coverage exists in `test_complete_chain_read_beats_a_failed_tmc_read` and related tests, but T9’s regression signal for the TMC-complete + chain-unregistered path is weaker.\n\n### Ask for the author\n\nFix brittleness by tightening assertions (stable field checks, not bare timestamp truthiness), not by turning the root test into a smoke check or stripping T9’s metadata checks without equivalent coverage.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | No prod diff; traced removed asserts to merge/membership logic | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins/grace tests weakened while docstrings unchanged | — |\n| settled-check | Partial overlap with other tests; root+probe-False path not fully duplicated | — |\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post; downstream steps (Cursor/Ditto/suite) proceed per the bot’s gate order.",
