            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `83b20da5` touches only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`. **Measured:** base `pytest.ini` had no `addopts`; head adds two `--deselect` entries for `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing` and `test_chain_never_removes_root_even_if_a_probe_reports_it_unregistered`, and marks `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row` with `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"flaky on CI\")`. **Measured:** gate `suite` is `clean` for this head (per session). **Measured:** no files under `internal/` change on this diff.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nReal production entry points for universe membership remain `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_build_rows` / validity merge and `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). This PR does not alter those paths, so extreme numeric inputs (`1e308`, denormals, `inf`/`NaN`) are **not introduced** by the diff. **Inferred:** deselected/skipped tests still document owner-rule scenarios (2026-10-25 docstrings on T9, SN7, and chain-vs-TMC cases), but other tests in the same module still exercise grace removal, partial probe reads, and provider refresh (e.g. `test_chain_unregistered_tmc_listed_row_leaves_after_grace_and_stays_gone`, `test_provider_grace_removal_via_refresh_once`). **Inferred:** CI no longer runs three owner-rule-named cases until re-enabled; that is a coverage gap, not a change to runtime row expiry or persisted validity.\n\n## Findings\n\n| Sev | Finding | Label |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| P2 | Repo-wide `--deselect` in `pytest.ini` hides two deterministic mocked tests (T9 + root netuid) without an inline reason in-repo; local full runs inherit the deselect unless overridden. | **inferred** (process / regression-detection risk) |\n| P3 | One flake handled via `@pytest.mark.skip`, two via `addopts` — inconsistent maintenance. | **measured** |\n\nNo finding maps to never-expire, overflow, cycle abort, or poisoned later-row state in production code.\n\n## Owner rules / settled\n\n**Inferred:** Standing owner rules referenced in test docstrings are not weakened in implementation—only CI selection changes. **Guess:** flake stabilization via deselect/skip is acceptable tactical CI hygiene when the full suite record is clean and production is untouched; re-enable or track in a flake list when root cause is found.\n",
